Generate {{ num_docs }} realistic English financial document excerpts following these rules.

## Rules
- Each document must be independent with different parties and details
- Mark PII entities with the following XML tags:
  - <PERSON>full name</PERSON>
  - <ADDRESS>full mailing address</ADDRESS>
  - <ORGANIZATION>bank or financial institution name</ORGANIZATION>
  - <DATE_OF_BIRTH>date of birth</DATE_OF_BIRTH> (only when applicable)
  - <BANK_ACCOUNT>bank account information (bank name, routing number, account number, account type)</BANK_ACCOUNT>
- Text outside tags must be natural English prose
- Include various financial document types
- Bank account formats MUST vary across these patterns:
  - "Chase Bank, Routing: 021000021, Account: 123456789, Checking"
  - "Bank of America, ABA: 026009593, Acct: 987654321, Savings"
  - "Wells Fargo, Routing No. 121000248, Account No. 456789012"
  - "Citibank N.A., RT# 021000089, Account# 112233445"
  - Include credit union and international wire formats (SWIFT/IBAN) occasionally
- Date of birth formats MUST vary: "March 15, 1985", "03/15/1985", "15-Mar-1985", "1985-03-15", "DOB: 03/15/1985", "Born: March 15, 1985"
- Every document MUST contain at least one BANK_ACCOUNT entity
- Most documents should contain a DATE_OF_BIRTH for identity verification
- Mix name formats: first-last, with middle name/initial, hyphenated, with suffixes
- Addresses: full US/UK/Canadian format with street, city, state/province, postal code
- Each document should be 100-300 words

## Output format
Separate each document with `---DOC_SEPARATOR---`

## Topic examples
- Bank account opening form, wire transfer authorization, loan application, direct deposit setup, power of attorney for financial matters